  "decision_conditions": [
    "REASON:\r\nThe proposed widening of the entrance gate and creation of a new vehicular crossover would introduce an additional, unauthorised vehicle access point, resulting in harm to the appearance and character of the streetscape and the setting of the locally listed building. The proposal would disrupt the established boundary treatment, fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Barnsbury Conservation Area, and would contribute to an increased prominence of vehicle movement across the footway. The development is therefore contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021), Policies PLAN1, DH1, DH2 and T3 of Islington’s Strategic and Development Management Policies (2023), as well as the guidance set out in the Urban Design Guide (2017) and the Barnsbury Conservation Area Guidelines, which collectively seek to ensure high-quality contextual design, protect heritage assets, and resist new or intensified vehicular crossovers."
  ],
